  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This 4-star campsite is located in Antibes, between Cannes and Nice. One caveat though: several signals, described below, cast serious doubt on whether the establishment is still in business.</p>

      <div class="callout" style="border-color:#c0392b"><strong>⚠ Check before planning a visit.</strong> The British site ukcampsite.co.uk lists this campsite as "PERMANENTLY CLOSED", and maeva.com states it is "not currently open for booking". No recent customer review (2023-2026) could be found, and the campsite's official website no longer appears in search results. None of this confirms an official, definitive closure — these are signals, not proof. Before planning a stay here, call the campsite directly on 04 93 33 93 99 to make sure it's still operating.</div>

      <h2>What was known before this doubt</h2>
      <p>The campsite's policy (camping-antipolis.com, source now unreachable) stated: "Animals admitted: 4€/night — only one animal per accommodation — category 1 and 2 dogs not allowed." This information predates the discovery of the possible closure signal and is therefore not guaranteed to be current.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cap d'Antibes and its coastal paths are a few minutes away by car — once the campsite's opening is confirmed by phone.</p>
